gnome-ssh-askpass:
gnome-ssh-askpass: gnome-ssh-askpass is a GNOME-based passphrase dialog for use with 
gnome-ssh-askpass: OpenSSH. It is intended to be called by the ssh-add(1) program and
gnome-ssh-askpass: not invoked directly. It allows ssh-add(1) to obtain a passphrase
gnome-ssh-askpass: from a user, even if not connected to a terminal (assuming that an X
gnome-ssh-askpass: display is available). This happens automatically in the case where
gnome-ssh-askpass: ssh-add(1) is invoked from one's ~/.xsession or as one of the GNOME
gnome-ssh-askpass: startup programs.
